I haven't read or played any of the modules for about 6 years, but I       
remember them well - and they were fun and (IMHO) the finest, and funnest,
campaign ever. I think that it would make a really good Nethack/Moria type
game, though certain ideas from each game would have to be shared.
Monster stats would have to be slightly altered. Drow would, for instance,
might have to be more powerful than mind flayers. Also food would have to last
slightly longer, or be lighter, or more frequently found, or cadavers (ala
nethack) left by monsters. Things would have to be tweaked. Stats would
probably be Moria in style. Possibly there would have to be certain bars
placed on returning to different levels in addition to the ones already
listed(Starter dungeon =>Fortress1 =>F2 =>F3,Depths etc =>Abyss =>Ship)
Possibly a couple of handy earthquakes between various stages of the
underground. Also, the ship might only be accessable after completion of all
the doors. The number of Spellbooks might also have to be reduced.

Also it could be developed as a multi-player game, with a limit on number
of players(2-4). Even PC users would be able to play a two player game
over a network or Modem. Moria type levels would only be reset when no-one
is on them, otherwise players would encounter the same level. Monsters
would be much harder, and experience would be dished out in proportion to
the amount of damage done


Comments, Discussion,_Constructive_ Criticism welcomed -

Is it a lousy idea?
Is it worth me learning C for?
Is there absolutely no chance of it ever happening within the next 60 years?


